				<pubDate>Mon, 21 May 2018 05:50:25 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>thefriendlyvandal</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2064544</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>For a further explanation: I wrote <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/every-day-of-my-life-you-test-me">the first entry of this as a one shot a month ago</a> after hearing a funny tumblr audio post describing the bottledick situation. It quickly amassed 50 upvotes, which is 49 more than I expected. It also caused my first ever <a href="http://photosynthi.tumblr.com/post/173079016098/even-if-you-get-it-to-be-high-rated-youll-still">death threats</a> and <a href="http://photosynthi.tumblr.com/post/173039162753/fucking-dumb-bitch-sick-of-your-smut-shit-being">hate mail</a>.</p> <p>Tonight, a month after posting &quot;Second Date&quot;, I received the most potent death threat I've ever received from the same person <a href="http://photosynthi.tumblr.com/post/174099956208/worthless-worthless-worthless-worthless-worthless">calling me a worthless dumb bitch and telling me that I should go kill myself</a>, which is again, not the first time they sent me something like this. I responded saying that if this is about the stupid fucking bottledick kondraki tale again I would do backflips. It also just so happens that this same anon (I assume), who seems to think that such Filth as gay characters and a funny tale about dicks is destroying the wiki, also sent Clef a <a href="http://scp-l4-clef-alto-001.tumblr.com/post/174042323050/why-are-you-supporting-people-making-clef-gay-when">message asking how he could have the audacity to allow such gay content, how dare he</a>. Clef did not like this and published this tonight in response and it's fucking hilarious.</p> <p>So far <a href="http://scp-l4-clef-alto-001.tumblr.com/post/174103688870/youre-not-the-real-clef-never-will-be-never-can">the anon has delivered on his blog in response</a>. I'm sure there will be more of this strange bottledick anon to come.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
